/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (To transform our analytical findings into a practical business solution, we developed a real-time inventory optimization prototype that simulates a modern retail decision-support system. The prototype was designed and developed using Visual Studio Code as the primary development environment, with Docker utilized to containerize the application and ensure a consistent and scalable deployment process.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 81 0 R
/T (Prototype Development)
/E (Prototype Development)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The system architecture consists of a FastAPI backend responsible for data processing, business logic, and real-time data simulation, and a Next.js frontend that delivers an interactive user experience. Communication between the frontend and backend is enabled through APIs and WebSocket connections, allowing the platform to display continuously updated inventory records and alerts.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (Since access to a live retail environment was not available, a simulated real-time data stream was implemented, generating new inventory records every few seconds to mimic operational retail activities. This allowed the prototype to demonstrate how inventory risks, stock movements, and product performance can be monitored in real time.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The prototype integrates several key capabilities, including inventory monitoring, demand forecasting insights, automated alert generation, inventory optimization recommendations, and an AI-powered assistant that helps users interpret data and support decision-making. By combining advanced analytics with an interactive user interface, the prototype showcases how data-driven inventory management can improve operational efficiency and support smarter retail decisions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
